{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":81712895,"ns":0,"title":"Cover time","extract":"In mathematics, the cover time of a finite Markov chain is the number of steps taken by the chain, from a given starting state, until the first step at which all states have been reached. It is a random variable that depends on the Markov chain and the choice of the starting state.","description":"Time to reach all states of a Markov chain","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}